Many sources (such as Omniwhack's extinctioninist ascension post) seem to
imply that no AC below -127 can be reached. I've heard this blamed on the
signed char format used to store the variable. Being familiar with two's
complement, this sounded fishy to me. An 8 bit two's complement integer
would have a range of -128 to 127. I tried out AC:-128 in wizard mode and
it seemed to work fine. After that, it does wrap.

